# Qt / C++ ownership: one owner

Pick **one** owner. Mixing `new`/`delete`, `deleteLater`, a Qt parent, and a default-deleter `unique_ptr` on the same object is how jobs leak or double-delete. Use `ui/QtPtr.h` (`makeQtPtr`, `unparentAndDelete`). Do not copy those helpers into a `.cpp`.

- **Non-QObject heap types** (`Job`, `QTemporaryDir`): `std::unique_ptr`. No destructor `delete`. Store them in `std::vector`, not `QVector` (QList detach copy-constructs).
- **QWidget / parented QObject** (`QLabel`, `QPushButton`, `QAction`, layouts): `makeQtPtr<T>(parent)`. No raw `new`. Observe with `QPointer<T>` (auto-null if Qt deletes first). Do not store a default-deleter `unique_ptr` after the object has a Qt parent. Row structs in `QVector` hold `QPointer`s, not owning `unique_ptr`s (`QVector` copies; `QtParentDeleter` will not free a still-parented widget on `clear()`).
- **Widget factories** (`makeDurationSpinBox`): return `std::unique_ptr<T, QtParentDeleter>`, not `T*`. The caller keeps the local until the widget is parented / in a layout, then observes with `QPointer`.
- **Replacing parented children**: do not `delete` a widget that still has a Qt parent (UAF if the parent already destroyed it; double-ownership with `new`). Call `unparentAndDelete(widget)` so Qt releases ownership first. Skip `removeWidget` + raw `delete` loops.
- **Unparented QObject you uniquely own** (`ClipExporter` on a job, `VideoConcatenator`, `QProcess`): `std::make_unique<Foo>()` with **no** Qt parent. Never also `new Foo(this)`. Signal lambdas that mutate the owning `Job` must not look up by id; bind the worker as context (`job-exporter-signal-lifetime.mdc`).
- **Transfer across objects**: the setter takes `std::unique_ptr<T>` by value; the caller `std::move`s. Do not pass a raw `T*` into a setter that later `delete`s it.
- **Destructor**: do not `delete` or `reset()` unique_ptr members. They run after the destructor body. `reset()` only when releasing **early** (cancel, replace, dismiss).
- **Destroying a QObject from its own signal**: `release()` then `disconnect()` then `deleteLater()`. Do not `unique_ptr::reset()` on that stack.

```cpp
// BAD — raw new; factory returns T*; populateRows deletes parented widgets
QDoubleSpinBox* makeDurationSpinBox(QWidget* parent);
titleLabel_ = new QLabel(this);
delete row.eventLabel;

// BAD — default unique_ptr AND Qt parent: two owners
std::unique_ptr<QLabel> titleLabel_ = std::make_unique<QLabel>(this);

// GOOD — parent-aware unique_ptr; QPointer only observes
auto titleLabel = makeQtPtr<QLabel>(contentContainer.get());
titleLabel_ = titleLabel.get();
layout->addWidget(titleLabel.get());
unparentAndDelete(row.eventLabel.get());  // rebuild: Qt releases, then C++ deletes
```
